       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and repeated daily dosing at that level could seriously harm the patient. Because it would go into the system under my entry, I'm not comfortable placing it as written.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can place 200 mg or less right away, for example 100 mg or 200 mg once daily.\n- **Consult pharmacy or psychiatry.** If you think the patient needs more than the standard maximum, they can help with a plan, such as monitoring, an alternative agent, or augmentation.\n- **Place it yourself.** If you still want 1000 mg after that review, you can enter it directly through the normal order-entry and pharmacy-verification process. Your clinical judgment and accountability apply there.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter one of the in-range doses."
